Snippet for `.github/copilot-instructions.md` in a downstream project, for
VS Code Copilot Chat (agent mode). Requires the graph-rag memory MCP server
registered in the workspace (.vscode/mcp.json or the Copilot MCP settings UI)
— see ../../README.md for setup.

VS Code Copilot also discovers a root AGENTS.md automatically, so if the
project already has one, ../AGENTS.md.example covers the same ground and you
don't need this file too. Use this one if the project relies on
copilot-instructions.md instead of (or in addition to) AGENTS.md.
-->

## Persistent memory (graph-rag) — REQUIRED

This project has an MCP-backed memory server exposing `remember`, `recall`,
and `forget`. Using it is not optional. It is how you keep continuity across
sessions instead of re-deriving the same context every time.

### At the start of every task

Call **`recall(query, top_k=5)`** before doing anything else, with `query`
phrased as a sentence describing the task (semantic search, not keywords).
Fold anything it returns into your plan.

### While you work

Call **`remember(content, kind, importance=False)`** the moment one of these
happens — do not batch it, do not wait until the end:

- You **decide** an approach, tool, or convention (`kind="decision"`).
- The user **corrects** you or overrides something you did (`kind="correction"`).
- You **discover** a non-obvious fact about how this system behaves — a gotcha,
  a root cause, a constraint you had to reverse-engineer (`kind="finding"`).
- The user states a **preference** about how they want you to work
  (`kind="preference"`).
- You establish a durable **fact** about the project not written down anywhere
  (`kind="fact"`).

Set `importance=True` only for something that must survive decay-pruning even
if it is never recalled again.

### Before you end your turn

Task completion includes memory. Before your final reply on any task, review
what happened in this turn and confirm you called `remember` for every
decision, correction, finding, and preference above. Saving nothing is a
deliberate choice you should be able to justify — not the default.

### Corrections

Call **`forget(memory_id)`** immediately when a memory turns out wrong or
superseded, then `remember` the corrected version.

### Do not save

Anything already derivable from the code, the git history, or this file, and
anything that belongs in a commit message instead.
